#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:133
msgid "Debug Builds and Sanitizers"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:135
msgid ""
"Device debug information follows Cargo's profile `debug` setting by default. "
"With the standard profiles, `cargo build` enables device-debug mode and "
"`cargo build --release` disables it. This is independent of `debug-"
"assertions`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:140
msgid ""
"For example, turn device debugging off in a development build through the "
"workspace's `Cargo.toml`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:143
msgid ""
"[profile.dev]\n"
"debug = false\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:148
msgid ""
"Cargo provides only `DEBUG=true|false` to build scripts, not the exact debug "
"level. Any enabled level currently selects device-debug mode, including "
"`debug = \"line-tables-only\"` and `\"limited\"`. It also selects device "
"optimization level 0 unless explicitly overridden, even in a release profile "
"with `debug = true`. Automatic line-only mapping is not implemented. Use the "
"explicit `line` override below for optimized profiling. See Cargo's [profile "
"settings][cargo-profiles] and [build-script environment][cargo-build-env]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:157
msgid ""
"`CUDA_RUST_DEBUG` overrides the Cargo-derived default when building the app. "
"No per-launch `.compile_options()` call is needed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:160
msgid ""
"# Optimized device code with source lines for profiling.\n"
"CUDA_RUST_DEBUG=line cargo build --release\n"
"\n"
"# Unoptimized device code with source locations and inline frames.\n"
"CUDA_RUST_DEBUG=full cargo build\n"
"cuda-gdb --args ./target/debug/my_program\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:169
msgid ""
"The accepted values are `none`, `line`, and `full`. Unset follows Cargo; "
"other values fail the build. Cargo tracks changes, so no `cargo clean` is "
"needed. The setting is captured when the target `cutile-compiler` library is "
"built, not when the proc macro is built. A package-specific profile override "
"for `cutile-compiler` affects this shared default; an override only for a "
"kernel's crate does not. Setting the environment variable only when running "
"an already-built binary does not change device compilation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:177
msgid ""
"`CompileOptions::new()` and `CompileOptions::default()` inherit this build "
"default. Use `debug_info()` to replace it for one launch. It sets both debug "
"flags, so it can also turn off a build-time `full` default:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:181
msgid ""
"use cutile::tile_kernel::{CompileOptions, DebugInfoLevel};\n"
"\n"
"my_kernel(args)\n"
"    .compile_options(CompileOptions::new().debug_info(DebugInfoLevel::None))\n"
"    .sync()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:189
msgid ""
"Each option is part of the JIT cache key, so the modes do not share a cached "
"compiled kernel. The individual flags remain available, as does sanitizer "
"instrumentation:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:193
msgid ""
"use cutile::tile_kernel::{CompileOptions, DebugInfoLevel};\n"
"\n"
"// cuda-gdb: debug information, no optimization.\n"
"my_kernel(args)\n"
"    .compile_options(CompileOptions::new().debug_info(DebugInfoLevel::Full))\n"
"    .sync()?;\n"
"\n"
"// Profiler correlation: line-number information only, full optimization.\n"
"my_kernel(args)\n"
"    .compile_options(CompileOptions::new().debug_info(DebugInfoLevel::Line))\n"
"    .sync()?;\n"
"\n"
"// Compute Sanitizer: memory-access instrumentation.\n"
"my_kernel(args).compile_options(CompileOptions::new().sanitize_memcheck(true)).sync()?;\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:210
msgid ""
"`debug_info(level)` replaces both debug flags. The individual "
"`device_debug(bool)` and `lineinfo(bool)` setters change only their own "
"flag, leaving other inherited settings in place."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:213
msgid ""
"`device_debug(true)` passes `--device-debug` to the device compiler and "
"implies optimization level 0. An explicit `opt_level` takes precedence, but "
"`tileiras` currently rejects full debug information at optimized levels. The "
"frontend also stops hoisting bounds checks out of loops. Checks it proved "
"unnecessary or moved to launch time are unaffected; they never reach device "
"code in any mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:219
msgid ""
"`lineinfo(true)` passes `--lineinfo`: source-line correlation for Nsight "
"Compute and Nsight Systems without changing code generation. This is the "
"option for profiling optimized kernels."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:220
msgid ""
"`sanitize_memcheck(true)` passes `--sanitize=memcheck` for `compute-"
"sanitizer --tool memcheck`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:221
msgid "`opt_level(n)` selects `--opt-level` directly; the default is 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:223
msgid ""
"Full debug mode describes source locations and inline frames, not Rust "
"variables or values. Tile IR currently supports control-flow debugging of "
"unoptimized code but not inspection of user variables; see the [Tile IR "
"debug-info documentation][tile-debug-info]."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:228
msgid ""
"User helpers and methods retain their definition's source file and line when "
"inlined, including across modules. Core operations are attributed to the "
"user's call site. Multiple generated instructions can still map to one Rust "
"line; this is not a one-to-one mapping, especially with optimization."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:233
msgid ""
"Generated const-generic array bindings use the containing function or "
"method's signature as their source origin. Generated reduction bodies use "
"the reduction call's location, including its inline caller chain."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:237
msgid ""
"Checks moved to the host launcher report the original access and its inline "
"callers when validation fails, including in builds without device debug "
"info. If several accesses share one launch check, its diagnostic retains "
"each distinct source origin while the predicate is evaluated only once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:242
msgid "Profiling"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:244
msgid ""
"Use NVIDIA **Nsight Compute** (`ncu`, reports opened with `ncu-ui`) for "
"individual kernels: throughput, occupancy, register use, and stalls. "
"**Nsight Systems** (`nsys`, `nsys-ui`) shows the application timeline: CPU/"
"GPU scheduling, transfers, synchronization, and launch gaps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:249
msgid ""
"For source correlation, build with `CUDA_RUST_DEBUG=line`. Keep the Rust "
"sources available on the machine where you inspect the report. Profile the "
"built executable, not the Cargo build itself:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:253
msgid ""
"CUDA_RUST_DEBUG=line cargo build --release\n"
"ncu --target-processes all ./my_cutile_program\n"
"ncu --set full -o profile_report ./my_cutile_program\n"
"ncu-ui profile_report.ncu-rep\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:260
msgid ""
"Replace `./my_cutile_program` with your binary's path, such as `./target/"
"release/my_program`. An `ERR_NVGPUCTRPERM` report means this machine's GPU "
"performance-counter access needs to be enabled by its administrator; "
"changing line-info settings will not fix that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:265
msgid "Use Nsight Systems for CPU/GPU scheduling:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:267
msgid ""
"nsys profile ./my_cutile_program\n"
"nsys-ui report.nsys-rep\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:272
msgid ""
"Look for launch gaps, unnecessary synchronization, memory transfer overlap, "
"and whether independent kernels actually overlap on separate streams."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:274
msgid ""
"Tile IR display is separate from Rust source-line correlation. NVIDIA lists "
"the Tile IR Source view as a new feature in [Nsight Compute 2026.3][ncu-tile-"
"ir]. If it is missing, record the Nsight Compute and CUDA Toolkit versions, "
"compile options, cubin, and report before diagnosing a metadata problem. The "
"standalone Tile IR dumps above remain useful independently of that view."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:280
msgid "Regression Checks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:282
msgid ""
"The repository tests source provenance and compile-option cache separation "
"without a GPU:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:285
msgid ""
"cargo test -p cutile --test debug_info\n"
"bash scripts/test_debug_defaults.sh\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:290
msgid ""
"The second command requires `jq`. It checks Cargo profiles, independent "
"debug assertions and build-dependency settings, explicit overrides, and the "
"line-only mapping limitation. It also checks that changing the runtime "
"environment does not change the built default. Additional checks are opt-in:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../guide/debugging-and-profiling.md:295
msgid ""
"# Requires tileiras, nvdisasm, and readelf, but no GPU.\n"
"cargo test -p cutile --test debug_info "
"cubin_has_rust_lines_and_inline_frames -- --ignored\n"
"\n"
"# Requires a supported GPU and tileiras.\n"
"cargo test -p cutile --test debug_info kernel_executes_in_all_debug_modes -- "
"--ignored\n"
"\n"
"# Also requires cuda-gdb and timeout; stops at a helper's source line and\n"
"# checks its nested inline backtrace before completing the kernel.\n"
"cargo test -p cutile --test debug_info cuda_gdb_stops_in_cross_file_helper "
"-- --ignored\n"
msgstr ""

